{"id":60956,"ord":74,"n_segments":146,"prev":60955,"next":60957,"doc":{"id":"70980","title":"70980_Quinn Wilson oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Quinn Wilson","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/70980/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=70980"},"chapter":"Inside the Hines band","title":"Hines's drummers","category":"person_portrait","summary":"Wallace Bishop, Alvin Burroughs, Oliver Coleman, Kansas Fields.","period":"1930s","year_from":1930,"year_to":1939,"words":247,"start":[108,3],"end":[110,2],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=70980#s60956","tags":{"places":[{"name":"Beaumont","focus":0,"type":"city"},{"name":"Texas","focus":0,"type":"state"}],"venues":[],"bands":[{"name":"Earl Hines Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Earl Hines"},{"name":"Red Allen's band","focus":0,"leader":"Red Allen"},{"name":"Horace Henderson's band","focus":0,"leader":"Horace Henderson"}]},"people":[{"name":"Alvin Burroughs","qid":"Q449051","n":4},{"name":"Wallace Bishop","qid":"Q1692121","n":3},{"name":"Earl Hines","qid":"Q354883","n":2},{"name":"Kansas Fields","qid":"Q1349491","n":2},{"name":"Horace Henderson","qid":"Q1627876","n":1},{"name":"Oliver Coleman","qid":"Q21031686","n":1},{"name":"Marshall Thompson","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":14,"theme_name":"Drummers and drumming: who played what, and how","community":42,"community_name":"Great drummers: who they admired and why","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":108,"b":3,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Earl always had good drummers."},{"p":108,"b":4,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"Yesh, he did."},{"p":108,"b":5,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Wallace Bishop and later on --"},{"p":108,"b":6,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"Alvin Burroughs."},{"p":108,"b":7,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Alvin Burroughs, and Oliver Coleman, yeah. Did --"},{"p":108,"b":8,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"Kansas Fields played drums with him for a while, too."},{"p":108,"b":9,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Yeah. I heard Kansas a couple weeks ago. Well, he was at --"},{"p":108,"b":10,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"He was at the benefit, yeah."},{"p":108,"b":11,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"At your party. Sure sounded good."},{"p":108,"b":12,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"Yes, he did. He still can play."},{"p":108,"b":13,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"And he gets some of that same"},{"p":109,"b":0,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"sound that Wallace Bishop got."},{"p":109,"b":1,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"Yeah."},{"p":109,"b":2,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Marshall Thompson does too."},{"p":109,"b":3,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":109,"b":4,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"The snare drum."},{"p":109,"b":5,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"The snare drum."},{"p":109,"b":6,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"And the way of playing. Not Wallace Bishop, Alvin Burroughs, I get that sound that Alvin Burroughs got, that sort of muffled sound."},{"p":109,"b":7,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"Yeah."},{"p":109,"b":8,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"But did you have anything to say about the drummers?"},{"p":109,"b":9,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"No, I didn't."},{"p":109,"b":10,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Earl would --"},{"p":109,"b":11,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"He hired the drummers, and they worked out all right. I didn't have nothing to say about it, as long as we could get along all right, you know."},{"p":109,"b":12,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Yeah. I was noticing that last night, you know, as the drummers came and went, they're all very good, very good drummers. Particularly Alvin Burroughs. I first heard with Red Allen's band."},{"p":109,"b":13,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"Yeah. That's right."},{"p":109,"b":14,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"He was quite a --"},{"p":109,"b":15,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"He was quite a drummer."},{"p":109,"b":16,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"And a lot of chops."},{"p":110,"b":0,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"Yeah."},{"p":110,"b":1,"s":"MR. DE MICHAEL","x":"Where did he come from?"},{"p":110,"b":2,"s":"MR. WILSON","x":"I think he was born in Beaumont, Texas. And I can't remember -- I'm trying to think what band he was with first, in Chicago. Oh, Horace Henderson's band. Yeah, 'Rum Boogie.'"}]}